Date: Sat, 5 Sep 2026 02:06:35 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 11171/11362] [outer-loop] Correction: report diversity IN
 EFFECT, not enabled (REQ-ARC-WMTE-7040)

My first fix was the wrong repair and it shipped a regression. It reset
explorer._hybrid_diversity on every level-up, which mutates real search state
to correct a reporting defect and removes the explorer's own self-restoring
draw. The adversarial reviewer caught it; I verified its reasoning in source
before reverting.

The randomised draw runs only when the feature is enabled AND
_steps_since_progress exceeds _stall_threshold. That counter resets to 0 at
every new best level; the threshold is 150 and the supervisor window is 120. So
at the first window on a new level the draw genuinely is not running and the
arm's diagnosis was correct all along. The arm was never spent: its
precondition read the wrong variable. diversity_active was built from
_hybrid_diversity, which means enabled, where the precondition needs in effect.

The fix is now one field mirroring the draw's own guard, touching no explorer
state. A test asserts the reverted mutation has not returned. 8 tests, 4 of 4
mutations RED.

Framing corrected on the reviewer's evidence. I told the operator this cost the
supervisor a rung on every level, implying lost search capacity. The
behavioural gain is about thirty actions of earlier drawing per level, applied
mode only, since the draw self-restores anyway. The justification is instrument
correctness: this field is why every deep level in the ledger is missing
exactly this arm, which corrupted the exhaustion signal.

Also records the independent energy review: no new energy opportunity on the
live path, fourteen candidates rejected against named artifacts, no build
proposal, because the bottleneck is generation rather than selection. And a
verified step-6 gap: the S0-S4 structural-energy ban exists only as CLAUDE.md
prose, with zero entries in an exclusion manifest that carries 34
blocked_patterns for other scopes, so the guard cannot fire on it. Filed as an
operator decision rather than added, because it changes what the planner may
propose.

This commit waited on another agent's open mutation proof rather than closing
it. Noted in status.md that the gate stops this session while the conductor's
checkpoint path runs no hooks at all, which inverts the intended protection.

